 longitudinal studies</article-title><source>Psychol Bull</source><year>2000</year><volume>126</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10668348</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037//0033-2909.126.1.3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B37"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cummins</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lo</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The quality of rural and metropolitan life</article-title><source>Aust J Psychol</source><year>2000</year><volume>52</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>74</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>